WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.840
Last question today is from Jeremy.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:09.950
Jeremy says, Hey David, are you worried that
the Sanders Warren, uh, candidacy are going

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.170
to candidacies?

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:14.490
I guess I'm trying to sort of reread this
in a way that makes sense.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:15.889
Let me, let me reinterpret it.

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:21.310
David, are you worried that both Bernie Sanders
and Elizabeth Warren running, we'll split

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:28.670
the progressive vote if neither of them drop
out, allowing the other to coalesce the progressive

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:34.350
vote Sanders we'll have an early lead in delegates
if he does well in earlier states.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:39.010
I think that right now there is no reason
whatsoever to believe that both Bernie Sanders

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:42.490
and Elizabeth Warren running is going to hurt
the progressive movement.

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:46.650
In fact, I think right now there's a benefit
to both Bernie and Elizabeth Warren running,

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:51.110
which is that even though they are both considered
to be sort of the left, most candidates that

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:54.920
are running, they actually have different
approaches and different styles and different

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:55.920
policy ideas.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:03.270
Bernie Sanders comes more from the democratic
socialist, uh, of an enclave of the left and

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.860
he has moved to running a campaign of social
democracy.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:12.680
Elizabeth Warren comes more from the let's
tweak capitalism to better work for the middle

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:19.400
class enclave of the Democratic Party and
has moved to the left to a position of social

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.840
democracy that is also very close to Bernie
Sanders, but their approaches in terms of

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:29.830
policy are quite different when you look at
everything ranging from healthcare to education

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.200
policy to other things.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.620
Is one better than the other?

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.250
Well, I think Bernie is slightly too.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:39.820
Elizabeth Warren's left and I am more left,
so on policy, I'm probably slightly more in

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:44.050
line with Bernie than with Elizabeth Warren,
but Elizabeth Warren is running an awesome

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:45.870
substantive campaign.

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:51.330
She's going to red states and doing town halls
and talking to Trump voters and other conservatives

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:56.070
head on in a way that is a really great thing
to be doing and he's engaging directly with

00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:01.050
people who might never imagine that they would
vote even though I think she's from Oklahoma,

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:06.740
for a senator from Massachusetts in terms
of the sort of political space that Elizabeth

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.100
Warren occupies now.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:13.890
So right now Bernie and Warren running is
a really, really great thing.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.910
Eventually it's going to be sorted out.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:21.540
They can't both be the nominees and I believe
that they are both aware of the impacts of

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.910
each of their campaigns on the other.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:31.050
I believe that as the debates get going, as
the polling numbers start to firm up in terms

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:36.060
of how they will look as the primary start,
either or both of them are going to do the

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:42.200
right things and in the long run I think that
they are going to grow the total base of progressive

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.650
support rather than divide it.

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.780
And I think it's an absolutely great thing.

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:51.310
They both are people who understand pragmatic
realities.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:57.140
They are both people who, uh, want the movement
to succeed first and foremost.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.390
And I think they're going to do the right
thing.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.220
I am not worried about that whatsoever.

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:03.770
And the way I see it, you know, sometimes
people say, David, you know, when you see

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:10.510
other progressive hosts growing their audience,
do you feel as though they're your competition

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:13.120
and they're hurting you in some way?

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.120
The answer is no.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:19.200
I mean, on a practical level, people only
have a certain number of hours of the day

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.980
during which they consume media.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:28.819
So in some very strict sense, if someone starts
watching a half hour a day of something else,

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:34.000
that's a half hour a day of me that they may
not be watching.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.910
But I have a different approach, which is
that progressive independent media is such

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:45.010
a small thing relative to the larger universe
of stuff people can watch or listen to that

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:51.780
I see other progressive shows as growing the
pie rather than taking a bigger slice of it.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:55.670
And I think that there's a very similar analogy
to what's going on now with the progressive

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:59.560
movement within the Democratic Party and even
outside of it in the United States.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:04.959
If you disagree with me, If you think Warren
and Bernie running at the same time is damaging

00:04:04.959 --> 00:04:07.170
the progressive movement, I want to hear from
you.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:11.730
I will listen to any and all reasonable disagreements
with my position.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.269
Uh, that's it for today.

00:04:13.269 --> 00:04:14.940
We've got a great bonus show coming up.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.260
The show doesn't have to end.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:26.599
Now if you become a member or a patron, you
will get instant access to the bonus show.

